dated)', 'description': 'When canShortCircuit() returns false, the validator must evaluate every subschema even after a successful match. A mock subschema validator increments a shared counter; the test asserts the counter equals the number of subschemas.'}]}, {'group': 'AnyOfValidator - validation of a nested child node (non‑root location)', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'executionContext', 'value': 'mockExecutionContextNested'}, {'parameter': 'node', 'value': 'jsonNode({"type":"object","properties":{"inner":{"type":"number","value":9}}})'}, {'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': 'jsonNode({"type":"object","properties":{"inner":{"type":"number","value":9}}})'}, {'parameter': 'instanceLocation', 'value': 'JsonNodePath.root().append("inner")'}], 'expected': 'empty Set<ValidationMessage> (anyOf validates the child node correctly)', 'description': 'The validator receives an instanceLocation pointing to a nested property. It must correctly evaluate anyOf against the child node while preserving the proper path in any generated messages.'}]}]
